  "def-nagata-strict-transform"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [lemma-nagata-constructible-closed-support],\n$V(\\mathcal J_i)=T_i$ in $U$. The restriction equality from\n[lemma-nagata-extend-finite-type-ideal] consequently gives\n$|Z_i\\cap U|=T_i$, so $Z_1\\cap Z_2\\cap U=\\varnothing$. Apply\n[lemma-nagata-separate-closed-subschemes]. In the resulting\n$U$-admissible blow-up $\\pi\\colon X'\\to X$, the closure of\n$\\pi^{-1}(T_i)$ is contained in the underlying set of the strict transform\nof $Z_i$: the strict transform is closed in $X'$, and it contains every\npoint lying both over the preserved open and over $Z_i$ — in particular\nevery point of $\\pi^{-1}(T_i)$. The two strict transforms are disjoint,\nso these two closures are disjoint as claimed.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-constructible-closed-support",
    "lemma-nagata-extend-finite-type-ideal",
    "lemma-nagata-separate-closed-subschemes"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
